WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.280
David and a business partner review what happens if one of

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.100
them dies. If the company needs funds to replace the lost

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.200
services of an essential worker, key-person coverage can address that

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.320
business loss. The business generally owns the policy and receives the

5
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.640
benefit under that arrangement.

6
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.220
A buy-sell agreement addresses a different problem: how an ownership interest

7
00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.520
will be purchased after a specified event.

8
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.700
Life insurance can fund the purchase obligation, but the agreement

9
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:34.020
establishes the transaction. In a cross-purchase design, the owners typically

10
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:39.320
insure one another; in an entity-purchase design, the business generally owns

11
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:44.360
the policies. Do not assume a key-person payment automatically transfers the

12
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:49.233
deceased owner's shares. David also has pretax retirement funds in a

13
00:00:49.233 --> 00:00:51.613
former employer's four-oh-one-k plan.

14
00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:56.633
He considers an eligible direct rollover into a traditional individual

15
00:00:56.633 --> 00:01:00.893
retirement account. Direct payment goes to the eligible receiving arrangement

16
00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:03.773
and avoids mandatory twenty percent withholding.

17
00:01:04.613 --> 00:01:08.653
Moving eligible pretax funds into a Roth arrangement instead generally

18
00:01:08.653 --> 00:01:13.073
introduces conversion income. If an annuity is used inside the traditional

19
00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:16.633
account, the account already provides tax deferral.

20
00:01:17.193 --> 00:01:20.933
The annuity must be evaluated for its other actual features, charges

21
00:01:21.493 --> 00:01:25.853
and restrictions. Do not describe an additional layer of tax deferral

22
00:01:25.853 --> 00:01:29.313
as an automatic benefit of placing an annuity inside an already

23
00:01:29.313 --> 00:01:34.095
tax-deferred retirement account. Rosa and David want reliable retirement

24
00:01:34.095 --> 00:01:38.895
income but also need access to money for near-term expenses and

25
00:01:38.895 --> 00:01:43.255
emergencies. A recommendation that commits all their liquid resources to a

26
00:01:43.255 --> 00:01:47.535
long surrender schedule may conflict with those needs, even if its

27
00:01:47.535 --> 00:01:49.315
illustrated income looks attractive.

28
00:01:50.315 --> 00:01:54.755
Review the actual consumer profile, available alternatives, liquidity,

29
00:01:55.555 --> 00:02:00.295
time horizon, costs, surrender terms and the features supporting the

30
00:02:00.295 --> 00:02:05.095
recommendation. For a covered Maryland annuity recommendation, best interest

31
00:02:05.095 --> 00:02:10.775
includes the required care, disclosure, conflict and documentation duties.

32
00:02:11.855 --> 00:02:15.235
An agent's compensation cannot be the reason to put the consumer's

33
00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:19.635
interest second. The worksheet should explain why this specific arrangement

34
00:02:19.635 --> 00:02:24.975
fits the known circumstances, including what resources remain available after

35
00:02:24.975 --> 00:02:29.227
the purchase. Compare two fictional income quotes with identical starting

36
00:02:29.227 --> 00:02:31.267
funds and no other features.

37
00:02:32.007 --> 00:02:36.467
Pure life pays nine hundred dollars monthly while Rosa lives and

38
00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:37.547
stops at her death.

39
00:02:38.047 --> 00:02:42.557
A life option with a ten-year certain period pays eight hundred

40
00:02:42.557 --> 00:02:47.727
fifty dollars monthly, continuing for her life and guaranteeing the stated

41
00:02:47.727 --> 00:02:52.147
minimum payment period. If she dies after exactly twenty-four monthly

42
00:02:52.147 --> 00:02:56.907
payments under the second option, ninety-six guaranteed monthly payments

43
00:02:56.907 --> 00:03:00.327
remain for the beneficiary under these assumptions.

44
00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:05.407
If she lives beyond ten years, her lifetime payments continue.

45
00:03:06.127 --> 00:03:10.247
The certain period is a minimum guarantee, not the end of

46
00:03:10.247 --> 00:03:15.407
lifetime income. The quoted amounts are teaching assumptions; actual

47
00:03:15.407 --> 00:03:17.867
rates depend on the contract and its pricing.

48
00:03:18.687 --> 00:03:23.047
Now consider David's separate personally owned nonqualified annuity issued in

49
00:03:23.047 --> 00:03:26.981
2020. It has a ninety thousand dollar value and sixty thousand

50
00:03:26.981 --> 00:03:31.407
dollars of adjusted investment, with no earlier withdrawals, debt or other

51
00:03:31.407 --> 00:03:35.754
adjustments. Before annuitization, he takes an ordinary twenty thousand

52
00:03:35.754 --> 00:03:39.807
dollar partial withdrawal. The thirty thousand dollars of gain is reached

53
00:03:39.807 --> 00:03:43.967
first, so the full twenty thousand withdrawn is taxable income under

54
00:03:43.967 --> 00:03:49.027
these facts. David is sixty-four, so the ordinary age-based ten percent

55
00:03:49.027 --> 00:03:52.187
additional tax does not apply, but the income tax remains.

56
00:03:53.007 --> 00:03:56.167
This is different from a properly qualifying exchange of the annuity

57
00:03:56.167 --> 00:04:00.787
into another annuity. That exchange can defer current gain recognition while

58
00:04:00.787 --> 00:04:04.127
carrying forward the relevant investment, rather than creating fresh

59
00:04:04.127 --> 00:04:06.167
after-tax basis at current value.

60
00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:11.430
Across these cases, begin by identifying the person or business being

61
00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.870
protected and the event that causes payment.

62
00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:18.510
Next identify the legal arrangement, who owns it, who receives the

63
00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.430
benefit and which money is pretax or after-tax.

64
00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:26.910
Then apply the actual time limit, contract provision or Maryland duty

65
00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.610
before doing the arithmetic.

66
00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:33.550
Read the question's assumptions instead of carrying a rule from a

67
00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:35.490
different product into the scenario.

68
00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:40.890
During timed practice, flag difficult questions and return with the remaining

69
00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:44.310
time. Then review missed answers and the linked lessons.

70
00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:49.010
Course completion records study progress; applying knowledge to fresh

71
00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.250
questions tests understanding.
